  "label": "The child is mapped as the embodiment of urgent desire",
  "description": "The textual phrase 'i want it' is directly mapped onto the visual entity 'child', who is depicted with a determined, almost aggressive expression and a raised fist, symbolizing the impulsive, urgent desire for something. The child's visual behavior (grimace, fist) is used to represent the textual sentiment of wanting something immediately, creating an analogical mapping where the child becomes the visual representation of the desire expressed in the text.",
